{"url":"https://files.alkamelcloud.com/wec/results_noticeboard/14_2026/03_24%20Hours%20of%20Le%20Mans/006_Doc%206%20-%20BRIEFING%20NOTES.pdf","sha256":"8b28440b6aadce6b8c59d7d6116933551013c34052142bd430c7334cf099c39e","retrieved":"2026-11-24T11:27:17.854Z","pages":[{"page":1,"width":595.25,"height":842,"items":[{"s":"1","x":547,"y":792.7,"w":5.9,"h":11},{"s":"2026 – 24 HOURS OF LE MANS – Appendix to briefing notes","x":184.3,"y":804.2,"w":226.6,"h":9},{"s":"2026 24 HOURS OF LE MANS APPENDIX BRIEFING NOTES","x":67.3,"y":87.8,"w":460.6,"h":18},{"s":"PIT LANE PROCEDURES","x":42.5,"y":127.8,"w":117.5,"h":11},{"s":"1)","x":60.5,"y":153.8,"w":8.2,"h":10},{"s":"Maximum speed in pit lane: 60 km/h.","x":78.5,"y":153.8,"w":157.9,"h":10},{"s":"2)","x":60.5,"y":166,"w":8.2,"h":10},{"s":"Red / green at pit exit must be respected at all times.","x":78.5,"y":166,"w":223.8,"h":10},{"s":"3)","x":60.5,"y":178.3,"w":8.2,"h":10},{"s":"If the red light is on at pit exit: any car waiting at pit exit must stop before the RFID or 3 meters before the pit exit","x":78.5,"y":178.3,"w":473.7,"h":10},{"s":"line.","x":78.5,"y":190.5,"w":18.4,"h":10},{"s":"4)","x":60.5,"y":202.8,"w":8.2,"h":10},{"s":"Unless instructed otherwise by Race Control, cars will access the working lane 5 minutes before the start of a","x":78.5,"y":202.8,"w":474.3,"h":10},{"s":"session; and cars will access the fast lane 3 minutes before the start of the session. The same will apply before","x":78.5,"y":214.8,"w":474,"h":10},{"s":"opening the pit exit to access the grid before the race.","x":78.5,"y":227.1,"w":227.8,"h":10},{"s":"5)","x":60.5,"y":239.3,"w":8.2,"h":10},{"s":"From the moment cars are allowed in the working lane before a session, article 12 of the Sporting Regulations","x":78.5,"y":239.3,"w":474.1,"h":10},{"s":"applies.","x":78.5,"y":251.6,"w":34.3,"h":10},{"s":"6)","x":60.5,"y":263.8,"w":8.2,"h":10},{"s":"Cars can be stopped by scrutineering at any time; drivers must respect the signal of the scrutineers.","x":78.5,"y":263.8,"w":425.2,"h":10},{"s":"7)","x":60.5,"y":276.1,"w":8.2,"h":10},{"s":"It is forbidden to place timing devices and/or beacons less than 3 meters from the official timing systems.","x":78.5,"y":276.1,"w":449.5,"h":10},{"s":"8)","x":60.5,"y":288.1,"w":8.2,"h":10},{"s":"Pit lane markings must be removed at the end of the race.","x":78.5,"y":288.1,"w":245.3,"h":10},{"s":"GENERAL SAFETY AND INCIDENT PROCEDURES","x":42.5,"y":325.9,"w":237.6,"h":11},{"s":"9)","x":60.5,"y":351.9,"w":8.2,"h":10},{"s":"If during a Red Flag, Safety Car, Slow Zones or Full Course Yellow procedures, your car encounters a problem:","x":78.5,"y":351.9,"w":474.5,"h":10},{"s":"you must instruct your driver to clearly leave the racing line immediately.","x":78.5,"y":364.1,"w":308.7,"h":10},{"s":"10)","x":60.5,"y":376.4,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"In case of accident:","x":78.5,"y":376.4,"w":83.9,"h":10},{"s":"•","x":96.5,"y":389.1,"w":4.6,"h":10},{"s":"Do not stay on the radio: this can lead to unnecessarily deploying medical services or may result in a","x":114.5,"y":389.1,"w":437.8,"h":10},{"s":"Red Flag.","x":114.6,"y":401.4,"w":39.8,"h":10},{"s":"•","x":96.5,"y":414.1,"w":4.6,"h":10},{"s":"If the car cannot continue:","x":114.5,"y":414.1,"w":112.9,"h":10},{"s":"-","x":141.6,"y":427.4,"w":2.4,"h":11},{"s":"The driver, when safe to do so, will leave the car as soon as possible.","x":159.6,"y":427.4,"w":290.9,"h":10},{"s":"-","x":141.6,"y":440.6,"w":2.4,"h":11},{"s":"The driver must help the recovery operations.","x":159.6,"y":440.6,"w":192.8,"h":10},{"s":"-","x":141.6,"y":453.9,"w":2.4,"h":11},{"s":"Car must be left in neutral with the steering wheel in position.","x":159.6,"y":453.9,"w":262.1,"h":10},{"s":"•","x":96.5,"y":466.6,"w":4.6,"h":10},{"s":"If the car can continue: the driver must stay in the car so that the marshals can hoist the car to a safe","x":114.5,"y":466.6,"w":438.4,"h":10},{"s":"place.","x":114.6,"y":478.9,"w":26.6,"h":10},{"s":"•","x":96.5,"y":491.6,"w":4.6,"h":10},{"s":"If the Impact Warning Light also known as “medical light” signal is activated, the driver must be","x":114.5,"y":491.6,"w":438.2,"h":10},{"s":"examined by the medical services without delay.","x":114.6,"y":503.9,"w":206.8,"h":10},{"s":"11)","x":60.5,"y":516.1,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"When going through a gravel / run off area:","x":78.5,"y":516.1,"w":179.8,"h":10},{"s":"•","x":96.5,"y":528.9,"w":4.6,"h":10},{"s":"Zig-Zag your car off track and make break tests before rejoining to drop the gravel / dirt off the line.","x":114.5,"y":528.9,"w":416.1,"h":10},{"s":"12)","x":60.5,"y":541.1,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"If the car is stopped for technical reasons, the scrutineers will release the car when they are satisfied with the","x":78.5,"y":541.1,"w":474,"h":10},{"s":"repairs.","x":78.5,"y":553.4,"w":32.6,"h":10},{"s":"13)","x":60.5,"y":565.7,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"In Hypercar category, it is the responsibility of a competitor to ensure that the car is electrically safe at all times.","x":78.5,"y":565.7,"w":474.7,"h":10},{"s":"The car must either have the ERS operating light illuminated (green light) or have a distinctive sign (green hat)","x":78.5,"y":577.9,"w":474.1,"h":10},{"s":"visible to all. This sign cannot be removed until the ERS lights is green.","x":78.5,"y":590.2,"w":298.3,"h":10},{"s":"ON TRACK DRIVING STANDARDS","x":42.5,"y":627.7,"w":162,"h":11},{"s":"14)","x":60.5,"y":654,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"Respect across all categories.","x":78.5,"y":654,"w":128.3,"h":10},{"s":"15)","x":60.5,"y":666.2,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"Blue flags (Appendix H ISC Article 2.5.5.e)) are to be respected at all times.","x":78.5,"y":666.2,"w":318,"h":10},{"s":"16)","x":60.5,"y":678.2,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"Except during qualifying, it is up to the faster car to find a way to overtake in traffic: slower cars should stick to","x":78.5,"y":678.2,"w":473.8,"h":10},{"s":"the racing line. During qualifying if you are not on a hot lap, make sure you are using your mirrors, and do your","x":78.5,"y":690.5,"w":473.7,"h":10},{"s":"best to stay out of the way.","x":78.5,"y":702.7,"w":113.4,"h":10},{"s":"17)","x":60.5,"y":715,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"Discord may be used between competitors to anticipate blue flags in the dedicated Discord channel. It is the","x":78.5,"y":715,"w":474.2,"h":10},{"s":"Team Manager's responsibility to inform the driver about the traffic.","x":78.5,"y":727.2,"w":285.8,"h":10},{"s":"18)","x":60.5,"y":739.5,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"Track limits must be respected at all times.","x":78.5,"y":739.5,"w":183,"h":10},{"s":"•","x":96.5,"y":752.2,"w":4.6,"h":10},{"s":"Track limit violations will be monitored and listed on a timing page.","x":114.5,"y":752.2,"w":283.1,"h":10},{"s":"•","x":96.5,"y":765,"w":4.6,"h":10},{"s":"Track limits are counted by driver by session. The race is considered as one session.","x":114.5,"y":765,"w":357.7,"h":10},{"s":"Posted at: 10:29","x":31.9,"y":29.1,"w":92,"h":12},{"s":"Doc No.: 6","x":501.8,"y":29.1,"w":59.3,"h":12}]},{"page":2,"width":595.25,"height":842,"items":[{"s":"2","x":547,"y":792.7,"w":5.9,"h":11},{"s":"2026 – 24 HOURS OF LE MANS – Appendix to briefing notes","x":184.3,"y":804.2,"w":226.6,"h":9},{"s":"YELLOW AND DOUBLE YELLOW FLAGS – Appendix H of the ISC Article 2.5.5.b","x":42.5,"y":81.3,"w":380.1,"h":11},{"s":"19)","x":60.5,"y":107.5,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"A Waved Yellow flag(s) means danger.","x":78.5,"y":107.5,"w":160.7,"h":10},{"s":"20)","x":60.5,"y":119.8,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"Reduce your speed. Forbidden to overtake until clear of the green flag.","x":78.5,"y":119.8,"w":299.5,"h":10},{"s":"21)","x":60.5,"y":131.8,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"Double Waved Yellow Flags may also mean that marshals and/or vehicles may be exposed, drivers must be ready","x":78.5,"y":131.8,"w":474.2,"h":10},{"s":"to stop.","x":78.5,"y":144,"w":32.4,"h":10},{"s":"22)","x":60.5,"y":156.3,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"The onus of proving that any flag is respected is solely on the driver.","x":78.5,"y":156.3,"w":286.3,"h":10},{"s":"23)","x":60.5,"y":168.5,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"The Stewards may penalise a driver if the driver fails to meet any of the following criteria:","x":78.5,"y":168.5,"w":375.7,"h":10},{"s":"•","x":96.5,"y":181.3,"w":4.6,"h":10},{"s":"Not slowing down at the entry of the zone.","x":114.5,"y":181.3,"w":178.6,"h":10},{"s":"•","x":96.5,"y":194,"w":4.6,"h":10},{"s":"Not slowing down at the point of the incident.","x":114.5,"y":194,"w":193.5,"h":10},{"s":"•","x":96.5,"y":207,"w":4.6,"h":10},{"s":"Not slowing down from the point of the incident until passing the green flag.","x":114.5,"y":207,"w":322,"h":10},{"s":"SAFETY CAR","x":42.5,"y":269.3,"w":61.2,"h":11},{"s":"24)","x":60.5,"y":295.3,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"Weaving to maintain tyre temperature is forbidden in the area(s) affected by the incident(s).","x":78.5,"y":295.3,"w":389,"h":10},{"s":"25)","x":60.5,"y":307.6,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"Weaving to maintain tyre temperature is forbidden during the pass around procedures.","x":78.5,"y":307.6,"w":368.8,"h":10},{"s":"26)","x":60.5,"y":319.9,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"Maximum distance between two consecutive cars is 5-car length gap.","x":78.5,"y":319.9,"w":297.7,"h":10},{"s":"PIT ENTRY BEHAVIOUR","x":42.5,"y":357.4,"w":112.9,"h":11},{"s":"27)","x":60.5,"y":383.6,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"Regarding the pit entry closed light, in case of failure of the hardware system, Race Control will do its best to","x":78.5,"y":383.6,"w":474.1,"h":10},{"s":"inform the Competitors immediately via radio and message on the timing monitor.","x":78.5,"y":395.9,"w":349,"h":10},{"s":"28)","x":60.5,"y":407.9,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"For the purpose of Articles 14.5.2 (FCY) and 14.6.5 (SC), the pit entry closed light system is considered as a help","x":78.5,"y":407.9,"w":473.9,"h":10},{"s":"for the driver.","x":78.5,"y":420.1,"w":56.1,"h":10},{"s":"29)","x":60.5,"y":432.4,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"However, for the purpose of Article 12.2.1 if the light is activated, the light must be respected at any moment.","x":78.5,"y":432.4,"w":463.9,"h":10},{"s":"30)","x":60.5,"y":444.6,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"Driver changes are not allowed during emergency pit stops. For the purpose of driving times, i","x":78.5,"y":444.6,"w":408.6,"h":10},{"s":"f the pit lane is","x":487.4,"y":444.6,"w":65.3,"h":10},{"s":"closed at the moment a driver change would normally be required, the Competitor must wait for the first","x":78.5,"y":456.9,"w":473.9,"h":10},{"s":"opportunity to pit and must inform Race Control accordingly. This tolerance applies only to the stint concerned","x":78.5,"y":469.2,"w":473.9,"h":10},{"s":"and shall not apply to any subsequent driving time requirements.","x":78.5,"y":481.2,"w":277.3,"h":10},{"s":"STARTING PROCEDURES","x":42.5,"y":518.9,"w":122.8,"h":11},{"s":"31)","x":60.5,"y":544.9,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"Gaps between cars must be kept as constant as possible.","x":78.5,"y":544.9,"w":246.3,"h":10},{"s":"32)","x":60.5,"y":557.2,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"A maximum of 5 cars length gap will be tolerated between categories.","x":78.5,"y":557.2,"w":296.2,"h":10},{"s":"33)","x":60.5,"y":569.4,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"Drivers must drive in two parallel lines; no lateral movement is allowed before crossing the start line.","x":78.5,"y":569.4,"w":427.2,"h":10},{"s":"34)","x":60.5,"y":581.7,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"Once the Start is given, front row drivers may accelerate, and the cars behind may follow their speed.","x":78.5,"y":581.7,"w":429.7,"h":10},{"s":"35)","x":60.5,"y":593.9,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"No overtaking is allowed before crossing the Start Line.","x":78.5,"y":593.9,"w":233.8,"h":10},{"s":"36)","x":60.5,"y":606.2,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"Unless instructed otherwise, in case of a start behind the Safety Car: the Safety Car will leave the grid at the","x":78.5,"y":606.2,"w":474.2,"h":10},{"s":"scheduled race start time.","x":78.5,"y":618.2,"w":112.2,"h":10},{"s":"37)","x":60.5,"y":630.4,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"When starting from the pit lane, cars will be allowed to join the formation lap(s) under the conditions defined in","x":78.5,"y":630.4,"w":474.1,"h":10},{"s":"Article 11.2.1, to gain tyres / brake temperature.","x":78.5,"y":642.7,"w":202.9,"h":10},{"s":"38)","x":60.5,"y":655,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"It is forbidden to start any engine during the national anthem.","x":78.5,"y":655,"w":260.6,"h":10},{"s":"END OF SESSIONS AND END OF RACE PROCEDURES","x":42.5,"y":693.7,"w":260.7,"h":11},{"s":"39)","x":60.5,"y":720,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"Parc fermé and the operations allowed are detailed in the Sporting Regulations: no other work or checks may be","x":78.5,"y":720,"w":474,"h":10},{"s":"caried out.","x":78.5,"y":732.2,"w":46.1,"h":10},{"s":"40)","x":60.5,"y":744.2,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"At the end of a session, a team may be asked to stop a determined car on a specific point of the track to simulate","x":78.5,"y":744.2,"w":474.4,"h":10},{"s":"a medical intervention with extrication. This request will be done via Discord.","x":78.5,"y":756.5,"w":327.4,"h":10}]},{"page":3,"width":595.25,"height":842,"items":[{"s":"3","x":547,"y":792.7,"w":5.9,"h":11},{"s":"2026 – 24 HOURS OF LE MANS – Appendix to briefing notes","x":184.3,"y":804.2,"w":226.6,"h":9},{"s":"41)","x":60.5,"y":80.3,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"At the end of the race, if possible, we would appreciate that the overall leader leaves a gap to the car in front on","x":78.5,"y":80.3,"w":474.1,"h":10},{"s":"track to present the chequered flag, unless the lead car is still fighting for position.","x":78.5,"y":92.5,"w":350.3,"h":10},{"s":"42)","x":60.5,"y":104.8,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"At the end of the race, after having taken the chequered flag: do not overtake other cars.","x":78.5,"y":104.8,"w":373.6,"h":10},{"s":"GENERAL ORGANISATION & COMMUNICATION MEANS","x":42.5,"y":142.5,"w":270.8,"h":11},{"s":"43)","x":60.5,"y":168.5,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"During the race, most of the Stewards’ decisions will be referred to on the timing monitors.","x":78.5,"y":168.5,"w":384.7,"h":10},{"s":"44)","x":60.5,"y":180.8,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"The on-board Marshalling display must be operational – in case of failure, Race Control must be informed.","x":78.5,"y":180.8,"w":451.4,"h":10},{"s":"45)","x":60.5,"y":193,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"If you have communication (radio) problems, the Team Manager needs to inform Race Control immediately.","x":78.5,"y":193,"w":457.7,"h":10},{"s":"46)","x":60.5,"y":205,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"If changes are made on the cars overnight, inform the scrutineers as soon as possible.","x":78.5,"y":205,"w":366.7,"h":10},{"s":"47)","x":60.5,"y":217.3,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"Visit the FIA Anti-Doping Campaign ‘Race True’ website – http://www.fia.com/fia-race-true-e-learning.","x":78.5,"y":217.3,"w":434,"h":10},{"s":"48)","x":60.5,"y":229.6,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"ADC armband is worn by officials appointed by the Stewards. Antidoping regulations should be enforced by","x":78.5,"y":229.6,"w":473.7,"h":10},{"s":"competitors. Access cannot be refused to officials.","x":78.5,"y":241.8,"w":218.1,"h":10},{"s":"49)","x":60.5,"y":254.1,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"Please acquaint yourself with the Appendixes A, B and C of the International Sporting Code.","x":78.5,"y":254.1,"w":390.1,"h":10},{"s":"50)","x":60.5,"y":266.3,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"International Sporting Code and appendixes must be respected during Competitions.","x":78.5,"y":266.3,"w":364.2,"h":10},{"s":"51)","x":60.5,"y":278.3,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"Pit wall radio will be tested 10 minutes before the session and will remain online 10 minutes after the session.","x":78.5,"y":278.3,"w":466.7,"h":10},{"s":"52)","x":60.5,"y":290.6,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"Discord will be operational 10 minutes before the session.","x":78.5,"y":290.6,"w":248.1,"h":10},{"s":"53)","x":60.5,"y":302.9,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"In case of issue (TV, timing, discord, …): inform Race Control or an ACO pit lane marshal.","x":78.5,"y":302.9,"w":377.1,"h":10},{"s":"54)","x":60.5,"y":315.1,"w":13.4,"h":10},{"s":"Alkamel monitors are 